Revision history for Net-Async-Keycloak

{{$NEXT}}
    - Net::Async::Keycloak::Admin: list_all_users_f pages through list_users_f
      with first and max until a short page arrives, so a realm with more
      than 100 users is listed whole; list_users_f stays one request and its
      documentation now says Keycloak answers at most 100 users by default
    - Net::Async::Keycloak::Admin: find_client_f, find_client_scope_f and
      find_user_f fail with Error::Validation, without a request, for an
      undef or empty key instead of listing everything and matching nothing
    - Net::Async::Keycloak::Auth: a 2xx from the token endpoint without an
      access_token (a proxy's HTML page, JSON without or with an empty
      token) is a failed login with Error::API, not a cached undef token

0.001     2026-10-04 18:03:50Z
    - Net::Async::Keycloak::Auth: admin token as a future, shared by callers waiting at the same time
    - Net::Async::Keycloak facade on IO::Async::Notifier with OIDC and the Admin REST API, every method as _f, ensure_*_f with WWW::Keycloak::Diff
    - Live tests against a real Keycloak behind KEYCLOAK_LIVE_TEST
    - Concurrency: a cancelled caller never cancels a shared login or fetch; discovery and key fetches are shared; tokens refused together cause one new login
